KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ B under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ after construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Both assertions fail, with out-of-bounds reads: the thunk through which
V's table enters B::g subtracts V's offset in a complete B (32) from
`this', also when the table (virtual_table::V@D, or the construction table
copied from virtual_table::V@B) is installed in a D, where V lies further
from B.  The Itanium C++ ABI uses virtual thunks that read a vcall offset
from V's table; the front end's thunks for virtual bases use a static
offset (build_virtual_thunk_body).  The W189 build fails it the same way.
